      "body": "## Additional context and logs\n\nThe Graal PR Spring PetClinic gate is failing because embedded Tomcat hits missing runtime reflection metadata.\n\nAffected jobs:\n\n- Current defaults: `Weekly Spring Tests`, job `80600494789`\n- `--future-defaults=all`: job `80600660682`\n- PetClinic checkout: `spring-projects/spring-petclinic@a2c2ef994340d3970eb6db51247456a51bb161f8`\n- PetClinic uses Spring Boot `4.0.3`\n\nThe native image build succeeds. The failure happens when `./gradlew nativeTest` launches the generated native test executable.\n\nPrimary failure:\n\n```text\norg.graalvm.nativeimage.MissingReflectionRegistrationError:\nCannot reflectively invoke method\npublic java.lang.String org.apache.coyote.AbstractProtocol.getProperty(java.lang.String)\n```\n\nRelevant path:\n\n```text\nSpring Boot TomcatWebServer.disableBindOnInit()\n  -> Connector.getProperty(\"bindOnInit\")\n  -> Tomcat IntrospectionUtils.getProperty(...)\n  -> reflectively invokes AbstractProtocol.getProperty(String)\n```\n\nThis is not JaCoCo, not Docker/Testcontainers, and not future-defaults-specific. It is a missing reachability metadata problem exposed by PetClinic's Spring Boot/Tomcat startup path under strict missing-registration behavior.\n\nThe direct metadata suggested by the error is:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"org.apache.coyote.AbstractProtocol\",\n  \"methods\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"getProperty\",\n      \"parameterTypes\": [\"java.lang.String\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nI would also expect `setProperty(String,String)` to be needed next, because Boot sets `bindOnInit=false` after reading it:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"condition\": {\n    \"typeReached\": \"org.apache.tomcat.util.IntrospectionUtils\"\n  },\n  \"type\": \"org.apache.coyote.AbstractProtocol\",\n  \"methods\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"getProperty\",\n      \"parameterTypes\": [\"java.lang.String\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"setProperty\",\n      \"parameterTypes\": [\"java.lang.String\", \"java.lang.String\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nThe metadata repo already has:\n\n```text\nmetadata/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core/11.0.18/reachability-metadata.json\n```\n\nbut it does not register `AbstractProtocol.getProperty(String)`.\n\nSuggested test coverage: add or adjust the Tomcat metadata test to exercise:\n\n```java\nConnector connector = new Connector();\nconnector.getProperty(\"bindOnInit\");\nconnector.setProperty(\"bindOnInit\", \"false\");\n```\n\nThis reproduces the same Tomcat reflection path that Spring Boot's `TomcatWebServer.disableBindOnInit()` triggers.\n\n## System information\n\nGraalVM version: GraalVM CE 25.1.0-dev+9.1\n\nOperating system: Linux\n\nCPU architecture: AMD64 (x86-64)",
